coverage:
I read all of introduction, coordinates (uniform harmonic coordinates, heat matrices, cumulative comparison), pinching (Poisson replacement, radial invariance, two-center commutator, radial transport, sharp projection, directional estimate) and renormalization (field estimates, iteration, jet bootstrap, metric bootstrap, limiting chart). I checked the following computations by hand:
- the volume-drop identity mu(B_t) = (a-n)V - t^{n+1}A' and its telescoping;
- the weak radial cancellation identity (it has no Ricci term in weak form);
- the commutator algebra (h = BU + c + e, B + BC_z - C_zB, delta - c = O(s));
- the transport cutoff sign condition, with A0 = 2(n+4)/(R-1) on both subintervals;
- the scaling M'(U) = r^{2-n} T M T^T, giving D_{i,y}[du] = r^2 M'(delta·U);
- the inverse-increment spectral identity, B_l Q_l B_l <= C B_l, and the convolution/background sums with 4a < gamma;
- the heat shell coefficients k_h and the reversal of sums;
- the metric-step identity, including <J xi,(D_xi K)v> = -<D^2h(xi,xi),Kv>;
- the diagonal recurrence and the l2 bound, and the error sums giving sqrt(eps) H_k;
- the normalized jet change of variables and the 2^{1-m} slack;
- the inverse majorant recursion (numerically checked that delta_m -> 0 and that the convolution is bounded);
- the final Taylor/tail bi-Lipschitz bookkeeping.
I did not independently verify the cited RCD analytic facts (JLZ16 kernel bounds, Jiang14 gradient estimate, DPG18).
